    "linkedin:7bca5606ae62a3950286cea8": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Web Developer",
        "company": "Netrolynx AI",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4480922371",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "",
        "is_remote": false,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n Sierra is the leading platform for customer\\-facing AI agents, working with many of the world's biggest brands—including The GAP, Rocket Mortgage, SoFi, Sutter Health, and SoftBank—to revolutionize customer service and business growth. Headquartered in San Francisco, Sierra maintains a strong in\\-person presence while expanding its offices across North America, Europe, and Asia. The company's core values—Trust, Customer Obsession, Craftsmanship, Intensity, and a commitment to Family—are integral to its culture and operational approach. These principles guide Sierra’s team in delivering innovative solutions and fostering a collaborative, high\\-performance environment. Co\\-founded by industry veterans Bret Taylor and Clay Bavor, Sierra benefits from leadership with extensive experience at Google, Facebook, Salesforce, and Google Labs, positioning it at the forefront of AI\\-driven customer engagement technology.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a talented Frontend Developer to join Sierra’s dynamic team. In this role, you will be instrumental in shaping the user experience across our core product and marketing platforms. Your expertise will ensure a seamless, engaging, and accessible interface for users worldwide. You will work closely with cross\\-functional teams—including marketing, content, and engineering—to develop and optimize features that enhance user engagement and drive business growth. Your focus will be on building robust, high\\-performance web interfaces, developing content infrastructure, and championing best practices in performance and accessibility. This position offers a unique opportunity to influence Sierra’s digital presence while working in a collaborative environment that values innovation, craftsmanship, and user\\-centric design.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate will possess a blend of technical skills, growth\\-oriented mindset, and collaborative spirit. You should have experience working on marketing or growth\\-facing websites, with a solid understanding of business metrics like funnels, conversion, SEO, and analytics. Proficiency in modern JavaScript, TypeScript, and React (or similar frameworks) is essential, along with a keen eye for UI/UX detail. You should demonstrate a strong commitment to performance optimization and accessibility, with concrete examples of past work improving these aspects. Experience working with headless CMS systems such as Sanity, as well as familiarity with localization and internationalization processes, is highly desirable. Excellent communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with non\\-technical teams are crucial to success in this role.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Own the development and maintenance of frontend interfaces across Sierra's product and marketing platforms, ensuring a cohesive and polished user experience. Collaborate on feature development within the web app and contribute to website branding, layout, and functionality enhancements.\n* Build and enhance content infrastructure by developing and maintaining our CMS (Sanity), enabling content and marketing teams to manage content independently. Design structured content models, editing workflows, and preview/staging environments to streamline content updates without engineering dependencies.\n* Partner with marketing, sales, and operations teams to implement analytics tracking, A/B testing, and experimentation frameworks. Translate business objectives into technical features that can be measured and optimized for growth.\n* Support localization and internationalization efforts by developing multilingual content workflows, translation management systems, and infrastructure to ensure a high\\-quality experience for users worldwide.\n* Prioritize performance by managing Core Web Vitals, media optimization, and diagnosing issues related to layout shifts, lazy\\-loading, and render timing. Measure and improve site speed and responsiveness continuously.\n* Champion accessibility standards by implementing semantic markup, keyboard navigation, and screen\\-reader support. Ensure all components and pages adhere to WCAG guidelines, making the website usable for everyone.\n\n\n**Benefits**\n Sierra offers a comprehensive benefits package designed to reflect its values and support employee well\\-being. Full\\-time employees enjoy flexible, unlimited paid time off, along with medical, dental, and vision coverage for themselves and their families. The company provides life insurance, disability benefits, and retirement plans tailored to regional requirements. Parental leave, fertility and family\\-building benefits through Carrot, and wellness stipends are also included. Employees have access to complimentary lunch, snacks, coffee, and discretionary stipends to support personal and professional needs. Sierra fosters a supportive environment where work\\-life balance is prioritized, and personal growth is encouraged.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Sierra is committed to creating an inclusive environment where all employees and applicants are treated equally, regardless of race, color, religion, gender, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, pregnancy, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, citizenship, or any other protected class. The company values diversity and believes that a wide range of perspectives enhances innovation and success. Applicants are encouraged to apply regardless of their background or experience, and Sierra ensures a fair and consistent evaluation process for all candidates.",
